{
  "id": "29830_pusshu",
  "headword": "プッシュ",
  "reading": "ぷっしゅ",
  "romaji": "pusshu",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "push; press; promotion",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "push; press; promotion",
      "explanation": "A push — pressing a button, or figuratively promoting or backing something or someone. Also seen in プッシュ{通知|つうち} (push notification). Takes する to mean \"to push\" or \"to promote\"."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "29830_pusshu_ex1",
      "japanese": "ボタンをプッシュする。",
      "english": "Push the button.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29830_pusshu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{新商品|しんしょうひん}をプッシュする。",
      "english": "We're pushing the new product.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29830_pusshu_ex3",
      "japanese": "プッシュ{通知|つうち}をオンにして{最新|さいしん}{情報|じょうほう}を{受|う}け{取|と}る。",
      "english": "Turn on push notifications to receive the latest information.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Loanword from English \"push\". Two common uses: physically pressing, and promoting or strongly backing something.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- プッシュ{通知|つうち}: push notification\n- {強|つよ}くプッシュする: to push hard, to strongly promote\n- ボタンをプッシュ: to push a button",
